Z||000000||88formula||08-08-2001||09:48 PM||||Does the fiero have any torsional rigidity? My frame of my car flexes really bad over most iregularitys in the road. It creeks and squeaks too much for my liking. I don’t remember it doing that in the past. It has been a year since I have driven it. Maybe I’m just used to my Toyota Tundra or maybe the stiffer shocks along with the Polly bushings make the frame flex more. <P>Any thoughts or experiences you guys want to share with me?  <P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 08-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||08-09-2001||12:48 AM||||Yes, it has some, but an X-brace under the chassis would do wonders. I've thought about that.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||08-09-2001||03:49 PM||||Your radio must have been turned up loud not to hear the creeks and squeaks of a Fiero especially if you have a sunroof. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||08-09-2001||06:17 PM||||Actually my GT was rather quiet and rattle free until I drove it on the crappy roads around my house for a few months, it seems that the car "loosens up" after a while.||||reg||1
